{"id":"peapods-2025--second-attempt","slug":"peapods-2025","sub":"second-attempt","name":"Peapods","date":"2025-07-08","one_liner":"After the attacker's pair-1 exploit (+78.19 ETH) and three reverted pair-2 attempts, Yoink replayed the same 42-call recipe one block later and took 174,258 USDC with an 11.49 ETH bribe; it returned 126,892 USDC (90% after cost). No pending attacker tx is shown.","bot":"Yoink","race_type":"post-failure-replay","narrative":"Press (Phalcon/BlockSec, Quadriga) says the attacker's 'second attempt' was front-run by Yoink. On chain, the attacker ran the exploit on pair 1 (WETH market) at block 22873986 idx 4 and netted 78.186 ETH, then tried pair 2 (USDC market 0xca1154bb) in three consecutive blocks 22874007/08/09. Each pair-2 leg reverted inside the attacker's try/catch (outer tx status 1, no profit). Yoink's tx0 (22874010 idx 0, 12 s after the last attempt) has the same state-changing call sequence as all three attempts (42 of 42 calls, identical Morpho loan of 10,000,000 USDC, identical UniV3 swap and Curve exchange sizes) and its borrowAsset passed, taking 174,258.31 USDC. So Yoink adapted a landed, failing attacker tx and completed it. It did not pre-empt a pending attacker tx that we can show: the attacker's earlier attempts had already landed, the attacker's calldata run on the pre-Yoink state still reverts (debug_traceCall), and neither side's txs are in the public mempool archive. Yoink's tx did exhaust the opportunity (the attacker's later attempts 22874015/16 stop at 'zero token'). Per the publication policy (confirmed-onchain needs the bot to be first or to pre-empt a pending tx) this is a post-failure replay, not a headline win.","chain":"ethereum","verdict":"related-not-frontrun","t0_ms":1751972183000,"pre_merge":false,"premerge_note":null,"slot":12095680,"block":{"number":22874010,"hash":"0xff8c7495fbfaf7db037db8d18c0519f7bbfe7bfe241d83731f797d38a65c1bfa","ts_ms":1751972183000,"ntx":4,"builder":"I can haz block?","fee_recipien